  "question": {
    "text": "Calculate the work done when 2.5 mol of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> vaporizes at 1.0 atm and <math><mn>25</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . Assume the volume of liquid <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is negligible compared to that of vapour. Given 1 L atm = 101.3 J and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.082</mn></math> L atm <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ."
